```javascript
const note = {owner: null};
console.log(note.owner?.name);
```
The result is undefined instead of trying to read name from null.

explanation:
In badges.ts, Badge describes the shape of an object. badgeText is an actual function that runs. internalPrefix is not exported, so another module cannot import it by name.
```typescript
export type Badge = { label: string };
export function badgeText(badge: Badge): string {
  return "Badge: " + badge.label;
}
const internalPrefix = "private implementation detail";
```

In main.ts, import { badgeText } brings in the function. import type { Badge } brings in a type for checking only. Type-only imports and type declarations are removed from the emitted JavaScript; the function still exists at runtime.
```typescript
import { badgeText } from "./badges";
import type { Badge } from "./badges";
const badge: Badge = { label: "Reader" };
console.log(badgeText(badge));
```
